# Changelog

Versioning starts here — no history before this point was tracked.
Scheme: `X.Y.Z` where X = breaking change, Y = new feature, Z = fix/patch.
Ask before assuming the next number; check this file for the last one
shipped rather than guessing.

Version currently only tracks `frontend/app.js` (shown live in the HUD
in the bottom-left corner — that's the fastest way to confirm what's
actually deployed, faster than digging through git history or raw
GitHub URLs). Server/firmware versioning can be folded in the same way
later if useful.

## 0.2.0 — 2026-08-23
- Fixed: office's south wall now flush under primary bedroom's (was
  protruding ~0.84m/2.75ft past it) — `config/floorplan.json`
- Fixed: orbit drag direction, exposed as a single `ROTATE_DIRECTION`
  constant in `app.js` so it's a one-line flip if still wrong, rather
  than another guess-and-redeploy cycle
- Added: version tag displayed in the HUD, to make "did the last
  deploy actually land" verifiable at a glance
- Reverted: an earlier `MIRROR_X` east/west data flip that was the
  wrong fix for what turned out to be a control-direction issue, not a
  layout issue

## 0.1.0 — earlier (untracked)
- Initial floorplan.json + Three.js frontend replacing the placeholder
  box shell
- Proxmox CT bootstrap scripts (`deploy/`)
